Create a namespace metadata file  and save it into ${WAREHOUSE_BASE}/namespace_metadata
Then :

The commands of list namespace or list table read the namespace metadata file. Reading from the file could have better performance than listing directories on file system, especially  on Object Store, like S3。
Move the functions of namespace manager out of catalog. Hive catalog could also take advantage of the namespace manager to support multi-part namespace, to meet the requirement of multi-part namespace in Spark.
It could help to manage the Iceberg tables and namespaces without the help from a center meta store service like Hive MetaStore.

